From: psX Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: retain failed started UVD state for terminal restart

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

Canceling a running decoder can fault its queue before an operator's terminal
ordinary restart reaches amdgpu_pci_shutdown(). The dev5 healthy/first-close
restriction then deliberately parks instead of reaching the atomic ICC reset.

Keep the existing immutable opt-in, SYSTEM_RESTART, built-in Liverpool,
entered-backing, started-runtime and initialized-jobs requirements. Also require
the exact UVD IP block to have completed hw_init; started alone precedes the
boot ring test and cannot establish that boundary. Permit an
already-closed or failed queue by invoking the existing idempotent fault path.
It blocks further WPTR publication, preserves latched errors and quarantines
entered leases. Return without normal AMDGPU teardown, as on the existing
power-off terminal handoff. The platform's registered atomic ICC handler is
still required; no attempt to reset or recover the GPU in place is made here.

Power-off, failed-startup, forced/kexec, suspend, removal and reset guards are
unchanged. No DMA drain or physical faulted-restart acceptance is claimed.
Apply only after the frozen dev5 retained-restart.patch; preserve that input.

Base: exact 7.2.11-psx-ps4-baikal-uvd-runtime-dev5
Base-SHA256: 685e10d862634337217b4647b960b8b0e4613a95cceb59589e013d081fe5f534  drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime.c
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime.c
@@ -155,48 +155,47 @@
 		return false;
 
 	amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_fault(adev, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	dev_warn(adev->dev,
 		"PS4_UVD_RUNTIME EXPERIMENTAL_POWEROFF retained=1 teardown=0; continuing to system power-off\n");
 	return true;
 }
 
-/* Ordinary restart may retain backing until the platform ICC reset, but
- * only from a started, previously healthy runtime. This is no DMA drain or
- * permission to suspend, kexec, unbind, free, rearm or reset the GPU in place.
+/* Terminal ordinary restart retains backing until the platform ICC reset.
+ * A canceled process may already have closed or faulted this started runtime;
+ * neither state permits teardown, but both permit the same terminal handoff.
+ * Failed startup, forced restart, kexec and in-place lifecycle paths stay out.
  * The historical power-off exception above deliberately keeps its semantics.
  */
 bool amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_restart(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime *s = &adev->ps4_uvd_runtime;
-	unsigned long flags;
-	bool admitted;
+	struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip;
 
 	if (!ps4_uvd_poff || system_state != SYSTEM_RESTART ||
 	    reboot_force || kexec_in_progress ||
 	    !amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_retain(adev) ||
 	    !READ_ONCE(s->started) || !READ_ONCE(s->jobs.initialized))
 		return false;
 
-	/* A job fault sets closed before calling back to the runtime. Serialize
-	 * that window and claim failed==0 under the existing publication lock.
-	 * Lock order is jobs.lock then publish_lock; all existing fault paths
-	 * release either lock before acquiring the other or invoking callbacks.
+	/* started precedes the boot ring test; core marks hw only after the
+	 * complete UVD hw_init returns success. A failed startup still parks.
 	 */
-	spin_lock_irqsave(&s->jobs.lock, flags);
-	admitted = !s->jobs.closed && ps4_uvd_begin_close(adev, -ESHUTDOWN);
-	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&s->jobs.lock, flags);
-	if (!admitted)
+	ip = amdgpu_device_ip_get_ip_block(adev, AMD_IP_BLOCK_TYPE_UVD);
+	if (!ip || ip->version != &ps4_uvd_ip_block || !READ_ONCE(ip->status.hw))
 		return false;
 
-	ps4_uvd_finish_close(adev, -ESHUTDOWN);
-	amdgpu_ps4_uvd_jobs_fault(&s->jobs, -ESHUTDOWN);
+	/* Idempotent closure blocks WPTR publication and quarantines every
+	 * entered lease. Existing runtime and job errors remain latched. Do not
+	 * wait for a healthy/first-close owner, drain, reset or free any backing.
+	 */
+	amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_fault(adev, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	dev_warn(adev->dev,
-		"PS4_UVD_RUNTIME EXPERIMENTAL_RESTART retained=1 teardown=0; continuing to platform reset\n");
+		"PS4_UVD_RUNTIME EXPERIMENTAL_RESTART retained=1 teardown=0 failed_allowed=1; continuing to platform reset\n");
 	return true;
 }
 
 void amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_park(struct amdgpu_device *adev, const char *reason)
 {
 	amdgpu_ps4_uvd_runtime_fault(adev, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	dev_err(adev->dev,
 		"PS4_UVD_RUNTIME RETAINED reason=%s; cleanup blocked, full poweroff required\n",
